---
deadlock_detection: false
---

# wiki_install_first_run_vs_serve_tick: `bough wiki install` (a person's
# first-run bootstrap) racing launchd's own first `bough wiki run` tick
# on a brand-new project, before either has created the wiki directory
# (go/tests/model/README.md).
#
# Product:
#   go/plugins/wiki/install.go install() calls ensureWiki(p) and
#     writeSkill(p) directly, taking no lock.
#   go/plugins/wiki/run.go Run() calls ensureWiki(p) BEFORE it takes
#     .ingest.lock (tryLock), so the lock never guards ensureWiki
#     either; it only serialises what comes after (writeSkill, the
#     ingest, commit).
#   ensureWiki is a plain check-then-create, `os.Stat ...
#     errors.Is(ErrNotExist)` then `os.WriteFile`/`git init`, repeated
#     for three components (ingest.log, the index, `.git`), then
#     `commit(p, "wiki: initialise")` iff this call created anything.
#     `commit` stages with `git add -A`, skips when `git diff --cached
#     --quiet` finds nothing staged, and drops every git error
#     (`_ = git(...)`).
#
# So install() and a concurrent first Run() tick genuinely race
# ensureWiki with nothing serialising them: each's stat-then-write for
# a component is its own check-then-act window the other can land in.
#
# Abstraction: the three components collapse to one field, `exists`.
# Each is checked and created the same way, so a race on one is a race
# on all three; nothing downstream distinguishes them. `commit` is one
# step: git's own index.lock (an atomic O_EXCL create, not itself
# modelled) is what actually serialises two concurrent commits, and its
# content is idempotent — a second `git diff --cached --quiet` after
# the first's commit landed finds nothing new to stage — so from
# outside, at most one "wiki: initialise" ever lands even if both
# callers decide to attempt it.
#
# What this checks: not whether the directory ends up right (it always
# does — whoever loses the stat race still writes the same idempotent
# content) but whether the race can leave either caller thinking it is
# done while the component is still missing, or land two "initialise"
# commits. Both assertions hold on the product as written: the race is
# real (Seen can be "missing" for both) but benign by construction,
# because every check is paired with its own unconditional create.

role Wiki:
    action Init:
        self.present = False
        self.i_seen = "unset"
        self.t_seen = "unset"
        self.i_done = False
        self.t_done = False
        self.committed = False
        self.commits = 0

    # Installer's os.Stat: a snapshot, racing the Ticker's.
    atomic fair action ICheck:
        require self.i_seen == "unset"
        if self.present:
            self.i_seen = "present"
        else:
            self.i_seen = "missing"

    # Installer's create-if-missing + conditional commit, a separate
    # step from ICheck so the Ticker's own check/create can land
    # in between.
    atomic fair action ICreate:
        require self.i_seen == "missing" and not self.i_done
        self.present = True
        if not self.committed:
            self.committed = True
            self.commits += 1
        self.i_done = True

    atomic fair action ISkip:
        require self.i_seen == "present" and not self.i_done
        self.i_done = True

    # The Ticker's first launchd tick, same shape.
    atomic fair action TCheck:
        require self.t_seen == "unset"
        if self.present:
            self.t_seen = "present"
        else:
            self.t_seen = "missing"

    atomic fair action TCreate:
        require self.t_seen == "missing" and not self.t_done
        self.present = True
        if not self.committed:
            self.committed = True
            self.commits += 1
        self.t_done = True

    atomic fair action TSkip:
        require self.t_seen == "present" and not self.t_done
        self.t_done = True

action Init:
    wiki = Wiki()

# Neither caller ever finishes its own ensureWiki call believing the
# component is there when it is not: each's branch is either "I saw it
# present" (someone else already created it) or "I create it myself".
always assertion InstallerNeverFinishesEarly:
    return not wiki.i_done or wiki.present

always assertion TickerNeverFinishesEarly:
    return not wiki.t_done or wiki.present

# The two callers racing the same check-then-create can decide to
# commit at most once between them; git's own idempotent diff, not
# modelled here, is what a from-scratch rewrite without it would need
# in its place.
always assertion AtMostOneInitialiseCommit:
    return wiki.commits <= 1

# Both callers finish, however the stat race falls.
always eventually assertion InstallerFinishes:
    return wiki.i_done

always eventually assertion TickerFinishes:
    return wiki.t_done

# The directory converges regardless of who wins the race.
always eventually assertion Converges:
    return wiki.present
